    <imageSet>
        <name>Compressed movies of individual tilt exposures</name>
        <directory>/data/frames</directory>
        <category>micrographs - multiframe</category>
        <headerFormat>TIFF</headerFormat>
        <dataFormat>TIFF</dataFormat>
        <numImagesOrTiltSeries>6650</numImagesOrTiltSeries>
        <framesPerImage>6</framesPerImage>
        <frameRange>
            <frameRangeMin>1</frameRangeMin>
            <frameRangeMax>6</frameRangeMax>
        </frameRange>
        <voxelType>UNSIGNED BYTE</voxelType>
        <dimensions>
            <imageWidth>5760</imageWidth>
            <pixelWidth>1.38</pixelWidth>
            <imageHeight>4092</imageHeight>
            <pixelHeight>1.38</pixelHeight>
        </dimensions>
        <details>Unaligned movie frames of the individual tilt exposures. Each movie contains 6 frames and was exposed with 1.97 electrons per Å^2, or 0.3 electrons per Å^2 per frame. Movies are compressed and require the gainref file "CountRef_TS_TS_test_02_000_0.0.mrc" (uploaded in a separate directory) for motion correction. Each file has an .mdoc file associated that describes details of the exposure. These are found in the folder "mdoc_individual_tilts". In addition, the folder "tomostar" contains a .tomostar file for each tilt series that contains the information on tilt series alignment in Warp format (version 1.09). The folder "gainref" possesses the gain reference file to unpack and motion correct the tilt movie frames.</details>
        <segmentationList/>
        <micrographsFilePattern>data/frames/TS_*.tif</micrographsFilePattern>
        <pickedParticlesFilePattern></pickedParticlesFilePattern>
        <pickedParticlesDirectory></pickedParticlesDirectory>
    </imageSet>
